ments":1,"created_at":"2026-07-23T13:20:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T22:21:41Z","closed_at":"2026-08-19T22:21:41Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.7.1.stable.official [a13da4feb]\n\n- Not reproducible in: Not tested.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7900 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.31021.5001) - AMD Ryzen 7 3800X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 63.88 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIf a Camera3D is left in Preview mode when the project is closed, reopening the project and clicking in the 3D editor causes repeated errors:\n\n```\nscene/3d/camera_3d.cpp:495\nCondition \"p.d == 0\" is true.\nReturning: Point2()\n```\n\nThe issue does not occur if Preview is enabled after the editor has already opened.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new empty project.\n2. Create a Node3D scene.\n3. Add a Camera3D.\n4. Add a MeshInstance3D (BoxMesh).\n5. Enable Preview on the Camera3D.\n6. Save the scene.\n7. Close Godot.\n8. Reopen the project.\n9. Click in the 3D viewport.\n\nThe editor prints repeated errors from camera_3d.cpp:495.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThe issue reproduces in a brand new empty project with only:\n\n- Node3D\n- Camera3D\n- MeshInstance3D (BoxMesh)\n\nNo scripts, plugins or project settings are required.\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30308840/test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repi